1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,030
AI motion design just changed.

2
00:00:02,070 --> 00:00:02,990
Here's the catch.

3
00:00:03,152 --> 00:00:03,932
A year ago? Fair.

4
00:00:03,972 --> 00:00:05,552
Warped clips. Melting text.

5
00:00:05,592 --> 00:00:07,552
Your afternoon, gone in After Effects.

6
00:00:07,789 --> 00:00:09,569
Then Opus 5.5 dropped.

7
00:00:09,609 --> 00:00:11,769
People asked Claude Code for a showreel.

8
00:00:11,809 --> 00:00:12,669
One line.

9
00:00:12,799 --> 00:00:15,699
"Make a dynamic 15-second motion graphics video.

10
00:00:15,739 --> 00:00:16,679
Go all out."

11
00:00:16,973 --> 00:00:18,783
And got this. Kinetic type.

12
00:00:18,823 --> 00:00:20,203
Particle reveals.

13
00:00:21,008 --> 00:00:21,548
Even the sound.

14
00:00:21,588 --> 00:00:23,608
Written in code, synced to every cut.

15
00:00:24,234 --> 00:00:25,454
And not just one look.

16
00:00:26,317 --> 00:00:27,737
But plenty weren't one line.

17
00:00:27,777 --> 00:00:31,697
One viral one-shot had a 10,000 character prompt behind it.

18
00:00:31,737 --> 00:00:33,697
Skills. Examples. A proper brief.

19
00:00:33,737 --> 00:00:35,297
The gap is shrinking fast.

20
00:00:35,337 --> 00:00:36,437
Taste still wins.

21
00:00:36,883 --> 00:00:37,723
Want my prompts?

22
00:00:37,763 --> 00:00:39,943
Comment PROMPTS and I'll send you the library.
